               "caution":  "History shows memory stocks often peak well before quarterly profits do. Even with KRW 107.4 trillion in Q3 operating profit, November\u0027s 20% two-week NAND spot drop and Q1 2027 consumer contract-price cut forecasts warn that non-AI memory demand is already softening. Add KRW 84.4 trillion in annual CapEx, tightening U.S. export controls on Chinese foundry orders, and zero technical confirmation of a bottom—with shares still below all major EMAs and MACD negative—and catching a falling knife remains a real hazard.",
