                            "Surging memory costs pushed the DX mobile and appliances division to a KRW 0.8 trillion operating loss in Q3 2026.",
                            "Technicals are deeply bearish at KRW 178,100—over 20% below all three key EMAs—with foreign outflows still pressuring shares."
                        ],
               "fundamental":  "Samsung anchors the AI memory oligopoly alongside SK hynix and Micron, uniquely combining DRAM/NAND scale with in-house foundry production for HBM logic base-dies. On October 29, 2026, Q3 revenue climbed 127% year-on-year to KRW 195.3 trillion and operating profit hit a record KRW 107.4 trillion (55.0% margin). Semiconductors generated KRW 147.1 trillion in revenue and KRW 106.5 trillion in profit as HBM4 tripled sequentially to 60% of HBM sales and 2027 HBM supply sold out. Foundry improved on 4nm base-dies and doubled 2nm project wins, supported by KRW 84.4 trillion in 2026 CapEx (KRW 76.8 trillion for chips). Meanwhile, high memory costs pushed consumer devices to a KRW 0.8 trillion loss. Despite November\u0027s NAND weakness and U.S. export curbs, the AI memory moat remains intact.",
               "headline":  "Record KRW 107.4T Q3 Profit Collides With Peak-Cycle Fears and Export Curbs",
               "news":  [
