               "opportunity":  "For long-term AI infrastructure holders, the disconnect between collapsing sentiment and booming AI fundamentals is striking. Unlike past commodity cycles, Samsung\u0027s 2027 HBM supply is already sold out under multi-year agreements, HBM4 now makes up 60% of HBM revenue, and 2nm foundry project wins have more than doubled alongside the Taylor, Texas ramp. If KRW 171,500–172,000 support stabilizes while HBM4 margins hold through 2027 and board buyback details arrive in late January 2027, the market may reassess peak-cycle fears.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "Most sub-scores look fair, but three warrant slight recalibration after Q3 2026. AI revenue exposure looks too low and should move higher: semiconductors drove 75% of revenue and nearly all operating profit while consumer devices lost money, making earnings overwhelmingly AI-linked. Market position also merits a modest increase as HBM4 reached 60% of HBM revenue with 2027 supply sold out. Conversely, bottleneck and pricing power should edge lower, since November\u0027s 20% NAND spot drop and YMTC competition highlight persistent commodity-memory cyclicality.",
