               "summary":  "Samsung Electronics trades at KRW 178,100 on 2026-11-23, down 52.4% from its KRW 374,500 52-week high, despite posting record earnings. On October 29, 2026, Q3 operating profit surged 783% year-on-year to KRW 107.4 trillion as HBM4 reached 60% of HBM revenue and 2027 HBM capacity sold out. However, a 20% two-week NAND spot-price drop reported on November 17, tighter U.S. BIS export rules pausing some China shipments on November 19–20, and peak-cycle fears triggered steep foreign outflows. The AI memory oligopoly moat remains intact, while technicals stay firmly bearish.",
